  "question": {
    "text": "<p>From the given transfer characteristic of a transistor&nbsp;in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CE</mi></math> configuration, the value of power gain of this configuration is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi></msup></math>, for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k&#937;</mi></math>, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k&#937;</mi></math>. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____.</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/08bef4ca-8afe-4122-95ee-3c6ef9ade9b4.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 232px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the current gain&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#946;</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in CE configuration is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Considering the third and the first points on the given graph, the current gain can be calculated as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>&#946;</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>300</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>100</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The formula to calculate the power gain&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>P</mi></mfenced></math> in CE mode can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Substitute the known values of the parameters into equation (2) and solve to calculate the required unknown parameter.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mn>100</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k&#937;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k&#937;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>1000</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>",
